	            }
	        }

		}

	}

}


// NOTE (AI): The NoSlow bypass in 50 lines. On pre update, while blocking with a sword, moving, on ground within 0.42, and with no active killaura target, it sends RELEASE_USE_ITEM with a BlockPos built from RandomUtils.nextDouble(4.9E-324D, 1.7976931348623157E308D) for every axis, then on post sends the C08 re-place at (-1,-1,-1) with the held item. The server only reads the status field of RELEASE_USE_ITEM, so the random position is ignored by vanilla, but it defeats anti-cheats that compare the C07 position against the player's location as a heuristic. The release+re-place pair cancels the eating/blocking slow without ever dropping the block state.

